    "text": "Encapsulation and Decapsulation: To send a message from one process to another, the UDP protocol encapsulates and decapsulates messages in an IP datagram. Queuing: At client site, when a process starts, it obtains one port number, one outgoing and one incoming queue. > Client process send messages to outgoing queue, UDP removes them one by one, adds UDP header, delivers them to IP. > If outgoing queue overflows, OS ask client process to wait before sending any more messages. > When a message arrives for a client, UDP sends the received datagram to end of incoming queue. > If there is no such queue or incoming queue overflows, UDP discards user datagram and asks ICMP protocol to send a port unreachable message to the server.",
